\par\par \b \uc2  Dlr up but capped by  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  fears, Clinton. \b0\par\par\uc2 474 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 Juni 1998\par 05:15\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par \tab \tab  0305 GMT\tab      TRADED HIGH/LOW AS OF 0300 GMT\par  USD/JPY     142.55/65\tab \tab    142.75-141.97\par  USD/DEM     1.7995/00\tab \tab    1.8002-1.7963\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par ---------------------------------------------------------------\par \f28 \par \par \uc2      TOKYO, June 26 (Reuters) - The dollar was higher against \par \par \uc2  the yen by midday in Tokyo on Friday, but its upside was capped \par \par \uc2  by concerns about possible dollar-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \par \par \uc2  Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  (BOJ). \par \par \uc2  The market was also wary about setting up fresh positions \par \par \uc2  amid U.S. President Bill Clinton's ongoing state visit to \par \par \uc2  China. \par \par \uc2  The dollar rose to its highest level since Japan and the United States surprised the market Wednesday last week by \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  jointly to sell dollars. \par \par \uc2  The greenback was lifted by buying related to setting up of fresh investment trust funds and speculative bids by some Japanese investors. \par \par \uc2  "We are likely to see more trust fund-related dollar demand early next week," said a dealer at a city bank, adding that such buying is also likely to be seen in European \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  But the greenback's rise was slowed by offers from Japanese exporters and investors, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "Overnight, rumours of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the New York Fed helped to push the dollar sharply lower, albeit briefly," said a dealer at a trust bank. "So the market is quite nervous about another round of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," he added. \par \par \uc2  But dealers said any \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is likely to have only short-term effects unless the government comes up with effective measures to clean up financial institutions' bad loans. \par \par \uc2  Japan's chief government spokesman Kanezo Muraoka said on Thursday that more meetings will be needed to work out a decision on the bridge bank, which is under discussion for the purpose of clearing up banks' bad loans. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the market was still cautious about chasing up the dollar during Clinton's trip, which lasts until July 3. \par \par \uc2  Clinton will meet Chinese President Jiang Zemin on Saturday. \par \par \uc2  "A weak yen certainly is not a good background for the Clinton-Jiang summit. So we need to be cautious about any remarks from U.S. officials," said a dealer at a city bank. \par \par \uc2  China's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor Dai Xianglong said on Friday he was very happy with last week's joint Japanese and U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the yen. \par \par \uc2  "We were very happy with the joint \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the United States and \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  to help support the yen," Dai told U.S. Treasury Secretary Robert Rubin in the presence of reporters before they began a closed-door meeting. \par \par \uc2  The dollar later extended gains, rising as high as around 142.95 yen, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The dollar closed at 142.05/10 yen and 1.7975/85 marks in New York on Thursday. ((Tokyo Treasury Desk +81-3 3432 9780 tokyo.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010925du6q022eu\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
