\par\par \b \uc2  Early Taiwan dollar slips further on yen. \b0\par\par\uc2 542 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 Juni 1998\par 03:47\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TAIPEI, June 26 (Reuters) - The Taiwan dollar opened higher on Friday but swiftly turned to fall sharply as the Japanese yen continued to wane below 142 overseas, dealersd said. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said after the opening high of T$34.100 orchestrated by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the Taiwan dollar began an early morning slide and by 0200 GMT, it was quoted at T$34.690. In early trade, the local unit had slipped as far as T$34.700 to the U.S. dollar against Thursday's T$34.457 close. \par \par \uc2  Turnover through dealers was modest at US$37 million. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said that while the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has determined to keep the rate up, there was little they could do but give the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  more room on its downside as the yen weakened. \par \par \uc2  "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  wants to break the link between the Taiwan dollar and the Japanese yen, but there is really no way to do that," dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Dealers felt the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would at some point step in to limit the fall. \par \par \uc2  "I don't think they will hold the rate back too much, but they will definitely keep an eye on it," said a local bank dollar trader. \par \par \uc2  The yen continued its fall overnight in New York, touching 142.75, and was trading around 142.55/65 in the Tokyo morning. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's decision not to adjust banks' reserve requirements at a quarterly board meeting on Thursday showed that the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  remained its main focus. \par \par \uc2  "Right now as the yen continues to fall there is no way the bank could adjust the ratios," one dealer said. \par \par \uc2  Dealers expressed frustration with the bank's fixation on the Taiwan dollar, saying this was distorting the market. \par \par \uc2  "Every day they open the market higher with these prices that no one can afford to take," one dealer said. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor Perng Fai-nan said after the meeting that the board had decided not to lower reserve requirements, fearing the move would have unacceptable repercussions on the on the volatile \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. \par \par \uc2  There was an undercurrent of anxiety that the yen's decline would trigger another massive coordinated \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the United States and \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Just such a move nine days ago buoyed the Japanese unit by more than six yen against the U.S. dollar, easing downward pressure on the Taiwan dollar. \par \par \uc2  Washington and Tokyo have said they could \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  again in the yen market when necessary, but Taiwan dealers said they were unsure if or when a further yen boost might come, citing Tokyo's apparent lethargy in addressing Japan's economic woes. \par \par \uc2  "Japan really doesn't seem like it's concerned about its own economy. The yen still has more room to fall," one dealer said. \par \par \uc2  "Lows near 146 are not that far away," he added. \par \par \uc2  The Taiwan dollar also was lower on Taiwan's second \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, Cosmos \b \highlight22\uc2 Foreign Exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2 , opening at T$34.560 against Thursday's T$34.455 close and ranging between T$34.540/700. ((Taipei newsroom, +886 2 2508-0815 fax +886 2 2508-0204, taipei.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    **..all news on Taiwan\tab    China\tab