\par\par \b \uc2  OPTIONS - Dollar/yen vols rise on spot jitters. \b0\par\par\uc2 338 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 Juni 1998\par 14:03\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, June 26 (Reuters) - Implied volatilies for dollar/yen options rose on Friday after the spot rate reached towards 143 yen overnight and fell back. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  options dealers said dollar/yen vols jumped as a result of concerns that the rise in spot had reached levels where it had last aroused \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  interest. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. Federal Reserve and the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  jointly \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in dollar/yen on June 17. Dollar/yen dropped to about 136 yen that day after hitting a session high of about 144.09. \par \par \uc2  "People are being cautious and a bit nervous," one dealer at a European bank said. "Dollar/yen vols are very high but they are still getting offers." \par \par \uc2  One-month dollar/yen options were trading at 17.90/18.30 percent compared to 16.20/16.70 percent in Europe on Thursday. One-month 25 delta risk/reversals remained in favour of yen calls at 0.45/0.75. \par \par \uc2  In the spot market, dollar/yen slipped back from an overnight high of 142.98 yen, its highest levels since the two central banks \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2 , after news that two major Japanese banks were planning to merge. \par \par \uc2  The merger of Sumitomo Trust & Banking and Long-Term Credit Bank of Japan (LTCB) is seen as a step towards financial reform in Japan. \par \par \uc2  Traders said dollar/mark volatilities were mostly sidelined by the market's pre-occupying interest in dollar/yen vols. \par \par \uc2  "That's all you have to write about today I'm afraid," said another dealer. "Everybody is just watching that. There is no other interest in anything else." \par \par \uc2  One-month dollar/mark vols were trading at 7.60/7.80 percent compared to 8.10/8.35 percent in Europe on Thursday. One-month 25 delta risk/reversals remained at mark calls around 0.1/0.4. ((Paul Casciato, London newsroom +44 171 542 8968 fax +44 171 542 5293, uk.\b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2 .news@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010925du6q020o5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
