\par\par \b \uc2  Signs of the bull still dominate dollar/yen charts. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Paul Casciato \par \uc2 622 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 Juni 1998\par 17:09\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, June 26 (Reuters) - Bullish signs on the technical charts are calling for a higher dollar/yen over the next few months in spite of a pullback on Friday and a sharp fall on \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  last week, technical analysts said. \par \par \uc2  Chart gazers pointed out that although \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  drove the dollar down sharply against \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's embattled \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  last week, it has crawled back to the upper band of a long-term bull channel. \par \par \uc2  "It is still inside a longer-term upmove and this still looks to be a short correction," said Ian Stannard, technical analyst at Chase Investment Bank in London. \par \par \uc2  A check of the monthly charts on Reuter graphics showed dollar/yen has been underpinned by trend line support drawn from its April 1995 post-war low of 79.70 yen. A parallel line drawn along the tops since then show the dollar in the upper half of a three-year bull channel. \par \par \uc2  A two-day short-term correction to the dollar's rise began on June 16 after it exceeded the top of the bull channel to reach near eight-year highs around 146.75 yen. \par \par \uc2  The break through the top of the bull channel was an indication that dollar/yen may be accelerating towards 160 yen over the next six months, rather than a sign that the end of the uptrend was nigh, chartists said. \par \par \uc2  They said a short backtrack on the daily charts showed the steeper trend began after the dollar recoiled from a multi-year high of 134.40 yen on January 7 to a three-month low of 122.35 on February 12. \par \par \uc2  A supporting trend line emerges at the February 12 bottom and has underpinned the dollar's recent move higher. A parallel rising resistance line can be drawn from the January 7 high, with a second touch on June 15 and confirmation of its trend at the June 16 multi-year high. \par \par \uc2  "That is an acceleration," said Allan Collins, head of technical analysis at Merita Bank in London, "I think we'll test 160 yen in the next six months." \par \par \uc2  Collins said an Elliott Wave analysis showed dollar/yen's rise has steepened as the result of a break to a fifth wave from the fourth wave. \par \par \uc2  "The fifth wave is generally the last one, the impulse one, the violent one and that is when it very often breaks out of the normal steady channel and you have a final kick up which is a lot more vicious." \par \par \uc2  Elliott Wave theorists believe that financial instruments chart their courses in series of five waves. \par \par \uc2  Analysts intimated that although the Federal Reserve and the Bank of Japan may have piggy-backed the technical correction to help push the dollar down last week, their \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  failed to provide an unusually significant fall. \par \par \uc2  "That's a typical reaction to a breakout, where you get a sharp move back," said Chase's Stannard. \par \par \uc2  In the midst of the technical correction on June 17, the U.S. Federal Reserve and the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  and drove dollar/yen down to a low of 133.60 yen, where it was stopped at the bottom of the accelerated trend, but not the longer-term channel. \par \par \uc2  "We're still very much in the upper half of the (bull) channel," Stannard said. \par \par \uc2  At 1500 GMT dollar/yen was trading at 142.68/78, down from an overnight high around 142.98 yen, but up from 139.19/29 in late European trading on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  ((London newsroom +44 171 542 8968 fax +44 171 542 5293, uk.\b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2 .news@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010925du6q01z2s\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
