\par\par \b \uc2  Early Tokyo: Dlr Jumps Vs Yen To Pre- \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Levels \b0\par\par\uc2 397 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 Juni 1998\par 02:24\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  TOKYO (Dow Jones)--The dollar jumped more than half a yen in early Tokyo trading Friday, breaking above levels where the U.S. Federal Reserve and the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  began coordinated \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on June 17. \par \par \uc2  Japanese institutional investors, banks and overseas funds rushed to buy dollars at the start of the Tokyo session, pushing the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  up to an early intraday high of Y142.70, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The buying was inspired in part by the lack of yen-supportive \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  late Thursday in New York, despite the dollar's rise to a high of Y142.35. That was the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's highest level since June 17 and puts the dollar above the level where the Fed and BOJ began their joint action to support the yen. \par \par \uc2  "Even though the dollar broke through levels where \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was conducted, there was no action by \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  authorities," said Minoru Shioiri, assistant \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  manager at Nippon Credit Bank. He said the lack of action reassured players about buying dollars. \par \par \uc2  The dollar may get a further boost against the yen if the dollar rises further and triggers stop-loss orders to buy the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which are said to be placed around Y142.90, dealers said. Such a rise could push the dollar above Y143.00. \par \par \uc2  But nervousness in the market about possible \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the BOJ and other central banks is increasing, particularly because of perceptions that an unchecked dollar rise would make last week's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  look like a failure - something monetary officials want to avoid, dealers said. Some dealers said even large profit-taking dollar sell orders could be mistaken for \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  action, resulting in wild swings in the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "It's likely to be very turbulent (Friday)," said a Japanese trust bank dealer. \par \par \uc2  Around 0020 GMT (8:20 P.M. EDT), the dollar is trading at Y142.45, up from Y142.38 around 0001 GMT and above Y142.10 in New York late Thursday. The dollar was quoted at Y141.03 late in Tokyo Thursday. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is also trading at DEM1.7983, higher than DEM1.7980 earlier but below DEM1.7985 late Thursday in New York. The dollar was at DEM1.7969 in Tokyo late Thursday. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) Dow Jones Newswires 26-06-98 \par \par \uc2  0024GMT \par \par \uc2  1074 1863 4162 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du6q05g62\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
