\par\par \b \uc2  Early Tokyo: Dlr Slightly Up Vs Yen On Institution Buying \b0\par\par\uc2 346 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 Juni 1998\par 03:06\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  TOKYO (Dow Jones)--Dollar-buying interest from Japanese institutional investors outweighed a flurry of yen-supportive comments made by Japan \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  officials, pushing the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  slightly higher in early Tokyo trading Thursday compared with its levels late in New York Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  The dollar is slightly lower against the Deutsche mark. \par \par \uc2  Eisuke Sakakibara, vice minister for international affairs, said \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets as appropriate. He also said the ministry remains in close contact with counterparts in Group of Seven nations and Asian countries. \par \par \uc2  A few minutes later, Haruhiko Kuroda, the head of the international bureau at the finance ministry, said that he is "concerned" about recent movements in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets, and is closely watching the situation. \par \par \uc2  The remarks dragged the dollar down to an intraday low of Y141.05 at 0027 GMT, but buying on dips by institutional investors soon emerged to push the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  back to around Y141.30. \par \par \uc2  "We are going to get more of these warnings from Japanese authorities" as the dollar approaches the next key target of Y142, said Koichi Udagawa, assistant manager of treasury and securities division at Daiwa Bank. \par \par \uc2  But many traders said the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  looks set to test Y142 in any case - a level near which \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  began last Wednesday, although the test may not come as soon as Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Around 0053 GMT (8:53 p.m. EDT), the dollar was trading at Y141.42, up from Y141.38 around 0001 GMT and above Y141.23 in New York late Wednesday. The dollar was quoted at Y140.86 late in Tokyo Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was also trading at DEM1.7997, lower than DEM1.8032 earlier and below DEM1.8035 late Wednesday in New York. The dollar was at DEM1.8018 in Tokyo late Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  The dollar is seen trading between Y141.00-Y142.00 and DEM1.7970-DEM1.8050 for the rest of the Asian day. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) Dow Jones Newswires 25-06-98 \par \par \uc2  0106GMT \par \par \uc2  1074 1863 4162 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du6p05ep9\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
