\par\par \b \uc2  Tokyo Midday: Dlr Up On Japanese Institutional Buying \b0\par\par\uc2 317 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 Juni 1998\par 04:21\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  TOKYO (Dow Jones)--Strong buying support from the Y139.30-level by Japanese institutional investors, setting up investment trusts, pushed the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  up against the yen midday in Tokyo Wednesday although the specter of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  may cap the dollar as it tries to go above Y140. \par \par \uc2  "The only way to change the direction (of the dollar) is to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 , although even that fear is lessening," said Ryohei Muramatsu, treasury manager at Commerzbank. \par \par \uc2  Indeed many dealers said the U.S. may not choose to join Japan in selling dollars as it did last week without more concrete plans from Japan on its promises to shore up the economic and financial system. However, unilateral action on the part of Japanese authorities remains a distinct possibility, traders said. \par \par \uc2  "Market players are very cautious above Y139.50 of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Shuji Takano, a dealer at ABN-Amro Bank, adding that U.S. players were interested in profit-taking around Y139.70. He said U.S.-\b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  joint \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was out of the question during Tokyo trading and unlikely in New York. \par \par \uc2  Given the market's cautiousness, \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  by itself would have an impact, but the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may be waiting for the traders to build up more long positions before jumping in, Commerzbank's Muramatsu said. \par \par \uc2  Around 0215 GMT (10:15 p.m. EDT), the dollar is trading at Y139.83, up from Y139.43 around 0030 GMT and above Y139.32 in New York late Tuesday. The dollar was at Y137.85 in Tokyo late Tuesday. It is also trading at DEM1.8015, lower than DEM1.8022 earlier in Tokyo and below DEM1.8018 late Tuesday in New York. The dollar was at DEM1.7935 in Tokyo late Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) Dow Jones Newswires 24-06-98 \par \par \uc2  0221GMT \par \par \uc2  1074 1863 4162 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du6o05deh\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
