\par\par \b \uc2  Early Taiwan dlr lower as yen falls below 139. \b0\par\par\uc2 346 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 Juni 1998\par 03:24\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TAIPEI, June 24 (Reuters) - The Taiwan dollar moved lower in early Tuesday trade with caution, dealers said, as the Japanese yen slipped below 139 overseas. \par \par \uc2  The Taiwan dollar opened slightly higher at T$34.196, but shortly afterwards it began falling to as low as T$34.380 to the U.S. dollar in early trade. At 0145 GMT the local unit was quoted at T$34.352 against Tuesday's T$34.202 close. \par \par \uc2  Turnover through dealers was modest at US$28 million. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said that the yen's fall overnight and in the morning was helping move the local unit lower. \par \par \uc2  "Although the Taiwan dollar isn't following the movements of the yen exactly, it's giving the Taiwan dollar more room on its downside," one dealer said. \par \par \uc2  The yen was quoted sharply lower at its Tokyo opening on Wednesday at 139.60-92 to the U.S. dollar against its Tuesday Tokyo close of 137.74-76. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's presence in the market and Taiwan's stronger fundamentals prevented the Taiwan dollar from falling as far as the yen. \par \par \uc2  "Taiwan still has stronger fundamentals than \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," the delaer said. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  over the past weeks has left the market in a state of anxious anticipation, scaring many investors out of long U.S. dollar positions. \par \par \uc2  "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has shaken things up so hard that no one knows what will happen next and when the bank will prop the rate up again," another dealer said. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said they expected the Taiwan dollar to trade in a range between T$34.10-50, unless the yen falls further. \par \par \uc2  Taiwan's second \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, Cosmos \b \highlight22\uc2 Foreign Exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2 , opened at T$34.365 against Tuesday's T$34.240 finsh and was trading between T$34.365-415. ((Taipei newsroom, +886 2 2508-0815 fax +886 2 2508-0204, taipei.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    **..all news on Taiwan\tab    China\tab    Hong Kong\tab .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (C) Reuters Limited 1998.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010925du6o029sx\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
