\par\par \b \uc2  Taiwan dlr ends lower as yen shows new weakness. \b0\par\par\uc2 475 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 Juni 1998\par 10:30\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TAIPEI, June 24 (Reuters) - The Taiwan dollar closed sharply lower on Wednesday, squeezed by quarter-end U.S. dollar demand and worrying new weakness in the Japanese yen, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The Taiwan dollar dipped as low as T$34.5 as the yen tumbled first through 140 and then 141 to the U.S. dollar, but regained some ground in the final minutes to end at T$34.352 to the U.S. dollar, still well below Tuesday's $34.202 close. \par \par \uc2  Turnover through dealers was modest at US$330 million, but US$55 million of it came in the final quarter hour - a clear sign, dealers said, of an \b \highlight22\uc2 interventionist central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The last-minute \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  boost, an increasingly common occurrance in recent days, confounded dealers. \par \par \uc2  "I don't know why the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  does this. If the rate is going to go down it will go down," one dealer said. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said quarter-end demand for the U.S. dollar remained brisk and questioned the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's apparent insistence on blocking further depreciation. \par \par \uc2  "Demand for the U.S. dollar is still very strong but no one knows what the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is going to do next," one dealer said. \par \par \uc2  "The market is like a pressure cooker." \par \par \uc2  Pressure on the Taiwan dollar intensified as the fading yen breached 141 - its lowest level since Washington and Tokyo joined forces for a massive June 17 \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  that propped \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  up by more than six yen. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said Taiwan's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  itself was adding to the pressure, noting that for the past two weeks, before and since the U.S.-\b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  yen \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been the major seller of U.S. dollars in the market. \par \par \uc2  "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  should let the rate depreciate some," one dealer said. \par \par \uc2  Dealers suggested the bank hoped to prove an oft-stated point - that the Taiwan dollar need not slavishly move with the yen because Taiwan's economy is far healthier than Japan's. \par \par \uc2  Dealers say investors still do see a link. \par \par \uc2  "It really doesn't matter what the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  does. There is still a linkage between the Taiwan dollar and the yen," one dealer said. \par \par \uc2  Dealers expected the rate would trend downward on Thursday as there was still heavy commercial demand for U.S. dollars that had been bottled up by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's actions. \par \par \uc2  "There still is plenty of room on the Taiwan dollar's downside," one dealer said. \par \par \uc2  Taiwan's second \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, Cosmos \b \highlight22\uc2 Foreign Exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2 , traded in a T$34.365/498 range and closed lower at T$34.445 against Tuesday's T$34.240 finish. ((Taipei newsroom, +886 2 2508-0815 fax +886 2 2508-0204, taipei.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010925du6o022rb\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
