\par\par \b \uc2  World  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2 : Dlr Extends Recovery, Edging Up Vs Yen, DEM \b0\par\par\uc2  By Masood Farivar and Nobu Kishi \par \uc2 379 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 Juni 1998\par 22:35\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  NEW YORK (Dow Jones)--The dollar rose against the yen and the Deutsche mark Tuesday, extending a slow but steady recovery from last week's joint U.S.-\b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Despite the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's impressive gains of the last two days, traders shied away from pushing the dollar above the psychologically-important level of Y140.00, fearing new \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  action. \par \par \uc2  Tuesday's advance brought the dollar to its highest level against the yen since last Wednesday when the U.S. Federal Reserve and the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market to halt the yen's precipitous decline. Though threats of further \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  action still exist, analysts say the further the dollar moves from the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  date, the bolder traders get to bid the dollar higher. \par \par \uc2  "With time the pain of last week's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  will erode and traders will likely bid the dollar higher," said Alex P. Beuzelin, market analyst at Ruesch International in Washington. \par \par \uc2  Late afternoon in New York, the dollar was trading at Y139.32, up from Y138.11 Monday in New York. The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was also trading at DEM1.8018, up from 1.7940 Monday. Sterling was trading at $1.6673, down from 1.6730. \par \par \uc2  What turned the tide in favor of the dollar after the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's failure to follow through on its pledges of new measures to clean up its banking mess and stimulate its economy. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  traders, who reward hard and fast action, reacted to that failure with disappointment, resuming their sell-off of the yen. \par \par \uc2  Instead of making good on those promises, Japan delivered more bad news Tuesday. The Economic Planning Agency reported that the index of leading indicators of the economy stood at 11.1 in April, the seventh-straight month it was below the boom-or-bust threshold of 50.0. \par \par \uc2  And rating agency Fitch IBCA said Japan's domestic recession, the Asian crisis, the decline in Japanese equity prices and the weakening of the yen have compounded the difficulties facing the Japanese banking system and could potentially undermine the sovereign's 'AAA' credit rating. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) Dow Jones Newswires 23-06-98 \par \par \uc2  2035GMT \par \par \uc2  1074 28038 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du6n05d2z\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
