\par\par \b \uc2  Fed's McDonough/ \highlight22\uc2 Japan \highlight\uc2  -2: In Contrast To April  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 304 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 Juni 1998\par 15:00\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  NEW YORK (Dow Jones)--\b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  didn't appear to sell U.S. Treasurys this month as part of its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  with the U.S. Federal Reserve to boost the yen, New York Federal Reserve President William McDonough said Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  "To best of our knowledge, there were no Treasurys sold," he said during a conference here on economic development. \par \par \uc2  Speaking to reporters, McDonough contrasted the recent \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in April, when it was "widely known" that \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold U.S. Treasurys to help it boost the yen. \par \par \uc2  McDonough also said Japan must seize the current window of opportunity to reform its economy and prevent it from spiraling deeper into recession. \par \par \uc2  "Japan would be very well advised to move in that direction," McDonough said. \par \par \uc2  McDonough traveled to Japan last week with Deputy Treasury Secretary Lawrence Summers to discuss economic proposals with officials from Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the Bank of Japan. \par \par \uc2  The trip came just ahead of a hastily called weekend meeting of finance officials from the Group of Seven major industrial nations to discuss ways to reform the Japanese economy and prevent its problems from adding further to the current economic weakness throughout Asia. \par \par \uc2  Chief among the G-7 concerns was that yen weakness would force China to devalue the yuan to prevent an erosion of China's trade position, thereby sparking off a new round of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  unrest in the region. \par \par \uc2  McDonough said he doesn't think China should devalue its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . "I believe it is not in China's interest to devalue the yuan," he said. \par \par \uc2  "It's not a question of whether they have to," he said, noting that China has a relatively strong economy which is still growing. \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 23-06-98 \par \par \uc2  1300GMT \par \par \uc2  4213 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du6n05cl9\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
