\par\par \b \uc2  Dollar off low vs yen in Tokyo but upside capped. \b0\par\par\uc2 537 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 Juni 1998\par 08:16\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par \tab \tab  0610 GMT\tab     TRADED HIGH/LOW AS OF 0600 GMT\par  USD/JPY     137.80/85\tab \tab 137.98-137.33\par  USD/DEM     1.7934/39\tab \tab 1.7946-1.7922\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par ---------------------------------------------------------------\par \f28 \par \par \uc2      TOKYO, June 23 (Reuters) - The dollar was down but off its \par \par \uc2  earlier low against the yen by late afternoon in Tokyo on \par \par \uc2  Tuesday, with the market's attention remaining focused on \par \par \uc2  Japan's bad-debt problems. \par \par \uc2  The greenback's upside was heavy due to lingering concerns \par \par \uc2  about possible dollar-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by central banks, \par \par \uc2  dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Earlier, the dollar fell as low as 137.33 yen on selling by U.S. fund operators and Japanese interbank players. \par \par \uc2  The dollar also came under slight downward pressure following remarks by Japan's Vice Finance Minister for International Affairs Eisuke Sakakibara, but the impact was short-lived. \par \par \uc2  "I think markets are underestimating the Japanese government's ability and determination," Sakakibara told reporters on Tuesday, referring to steps Japan has said it will take to boost its economy and stabilise its financial system. \par \par \uc2  "Overseas operators are still keen to liquidate dollar longs ahead of President (Bill) Clinton's trip to China," said a dealer at a European bank. \par \par \uc2  Clinton will visit China from Thursday to July 3. \par \par \uc2  "I think one of the strong motives that led to a joint yen-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the United States last week was their desire to dissuade China from devaluing the yuan," said the city bank dealer. \par \par \uc2  "So financial authorities are likely to prevent the dollar from going above 140 yen again, at least until Clinton returns from China," he added. \par \par \uc2  The greenback pared earlier losses on buying by Japanese investors and importers. Buying related to the setting up of fresh investment trust funds was also detected, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  But some Japanese investors who had bought dollars above 142 yen, were detected selling dollars for hedging purposes. \par \par \uc2  Despite persistent fears of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the dollar could slowly creep higher if the Japanese government fails to quickly come up with solutions for the banks' bad loan problem, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The market was cautious ahead of news conference and speeches by senior ruling party politicians later on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  Prime Minister Ryutaro Hashimoto is scheduled to give a news conference at 0700 GMT. \par \par \uc2  Koichi Kato, secretary-general of the ruling Liberal Democratic Party (LDP), will speak about current policy issues at the headquarters of Keidanren from around 0720 to 0820 GMT. \par \par \uc2  "The market is trying to determine how aggressive LDP officials will be in tackling the bad loan problem," said a dealer at a European bank. \par \par \uc2  A drop in Tokyo share prices also helped to underpin the dollar, dealers said. The benchmark Nikkei 225 average closed down 254.49 points, or 1.66 percent, at 15,054.60. \par \par \uc2  "Had it not been for fears of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , I think the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market would have reacted more straight-forwardly to the Nikkei's fall," said a dealer at a long-term credit bank. \par \par \uc2  The dollar closed at 138.07/17 yen and 1.7930/40 marks in New York on Monday. ((Kanta Watanabe, Tokyo Treasury Desk +81-3 3432 9780 tokyo.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010925du6n027ff\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw200\pich25\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3000\pichgoal375
