\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  Options:Tokyo Volatilities Up As Dlr Soars In Spot Mkt \b0\par\par\uc2 338 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 Juni 1998\par 07:08\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  TOKYO (Dow Jones)--Volatilities implied by yen \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  options shot up Monday in Tokyo after a weekend meeting of international finance authorities failed to result in concrete proposals to stem Japan's banking crisis or to support the yen. Deutsche mark volatilities are up slightly. \par \par \uc2  The dollar opened sharply higher than its levels late Friday in New York, at one point trading near Y139. Worries of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from the U.S. and \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the wake of last week's surprising joint action brought in some profit-taking, but the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  remained well-bid across the board. \par \par \uc2  Saturday's hastily called meeting of deputy finance ministers and \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  officials from the Group of Seven countries and 10 of the 11 members of the Asia countries in the Manila Framework resulted in a strong statement urging Japan to clean up its banking sector and revive its economy. However, the lack of specifics from Tokyo resulted in disappointment from \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  traders. \par \par \uc2  Market players rushed to set up knock-out options around Y140.00, and one-week yen option volatilities rose above 21%, as traders said the dollar would rise to that level, perhaps testing Y142, which is where the joint \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  started last week. \par \par \uc2  "Short-term yen volatilities are soaring," said a trader at a U.K. bank in Tokyo. "Buyers are everywhere." \par \par \uc2  In the over-the-counter market, one-month at-the-money dollar/yen options imply volatility of 18.0% bid, up from 17.5% in London Friday, and way above 15.1% in Tokyo Friday. \par \par \uc2  Against the mark, they are higher at 8.65% from 8.4% both in London and Tokyo Friday. \par \par \uc2  At 0445 GMT (12:45 p.m. EDT), the dollar is at Y137.40 and DEM1.7940, well up from Y135.83 and DEM1.7855 late Friday in New York. \par \par \uc2  -By John Brinsley; 813-5255-2929; jbrinsley@ap.org \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 22-06-98 \par \par \uc2  0508GMT \par \par \uc2  1077 4127 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du6m05azt\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
