\par\par \b \uc2  Tokyo Midday: Dlr Dn Vs Yen On Pft Taking, MOF Comments \b0\par\par\uc2 420 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 Juni 1998\par 04:27\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  TOKYO (Dow Jones)--Profit-taking by Japanese and foreign investors after the dollar hit an intraday high of Y138.35 early in Tokyo pushed the dollar down against the yen at midday Monday from its earlier levels. \par \par \uc2  The dollar is running into resistance ahead of Y139 as the market remains wary of additional \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the part of the U.S. and \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  following last week's joint action. With President Bill Clinton traveling to China this week, the U.S. may be obliged to defend the yen following Chinese hints to devalue the yuan if Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  continued to weaken. \par \par \uc2  "The market is presuming that the U.S. doesn't a weaker yen during Clinton's visit, as China started to complain about the weak yen around Y140," said Shuji Takano, a \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealers at ABN-Amro in Tokyo. \par \par \uc2  Earlier, disappointment that Japan didn't promise concrete policy steps to resolve problems in its banking sector at meeting of international finance authorities over the weekend spurred dollar buying across the board, but profit-taking after \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  officials hinted at further \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  brought the dollar off its highs. \par \par \uc2  However, the dollar should find initial support in the lower-Y137 range, with further support at Y135, traders said. \par \par \uc2  The meeting of G-7 deputies and senior finance authorities from 10 Asian economies put strong pressure on Japan to stimulate its economy and clean up its bad debt problem. But a lack of specifics from Japan could prompt the yen to fall again, traders warned. \par \par \uc2  "If the government doesn't move quickly, yen selling will start again," said Takano. \par \par \uc2  After meeting with Prime Minister Ryutaro Hashimoto, the ruling Liberal Democratic Party's secretary-general, Koichi Kato, said the government will make a final decision regarding the formation of a public "bridge bank" to take on bad debts from ailing financial institutions as a means to help stabilize the financial system by July 8. \par \par \uc2  Around 0215 GMT (10:15 p.m. EDT), the dollar is at Y137.33, down from Y137.50 around 0030 GMT but above Y135.83 in New York late Friday. It was quoted at Y136.95 in Tokyo late Friday. The dollar is also trading at DEM1.7942, higher than DEM1.7905 earlier in Tokyo but above DEM1.7855 late Friday in New York. It was at DEM1.7933 in Tokyo late Friday. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) Dow Jones Newswires 22-06-98 \par \par \uc2  0227GMT \par \par \uc2  1074 1863 4162 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du6m05ahs\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
