\par\par \b \uc2  =BOJ Watch -2: Mkts Want Quick Action On Bad Debts \b0\par\par\uc2 315 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 Juni 1998\par 13:55\par \uc2  Capital Markets Report \par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    The dollar jumped from around Y138.63 in late May to\par around Y145.45 in mid-June, while the Nikkei stock index\par plunged from around 15,670.78 points to 14,614.74 points\par during the same period.\par    The plunge was only reversed last week when the U.S. and\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  mounted a successful joint \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets.\par    The Nikkei closed Monday at 15,309.09, while the dollar\par was trading around Y138.40 - despite a fall in the yen early\par Monday following a disappointing weekend meeting of deputy\par finance ministers of the Group of Seven and various Asian\par nations. The meeting produced only vague promises of action\par by Japan.\par    Much now will depend now on how fast Japan acts to\par resolve the bad debts of its banking system and stimulate\par the flagging economy, analysts said.\par    Some analysts think it will take a while for new\par policies to emerge, spelling trouble for the markets.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    "It's possible for the markets, after a short pause, to\par shift their focus once again on the dire state of the\par economic fundamentals," said Tamotsu Yasuda, an economist at\par Bank of Tokyo-Mitsubishi.\par    Indeed, the tankan will likely reinforce the negative\par message sent by recent key economic indicators.\par    Gross domestic product shrank 1.3% in the January-March\par quarter, and the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Ministry of Finance\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's business sentiment\par index (BSI) - which subtracts the percentage of companies\par saying the economy is worsening from those saying the\par economy is improving - fell to minus 36.1 for big\par manufacturers during the April-June quarter from minus 31.0\par for the January-March quarter.\par    "The tankan will be a confirmation of the weak economy,\par which is consistent with expectations for another quarter of\par GDP decline," said Cameron Umetsu, senior economist at LTCB\par Warburg Securities Ltd.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (MORE) Dow Jones Newswires  06-22-98\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 0755EDT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument cm00000020010916du6m01itb\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
