\par\par \b \uc2  Dlr up by Tokyo noon after G7, but lacks direction. \b0\par\par\uc2 577 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 Juni 1998\par 05:19\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par \tab \tab  0300 GMT\tab      TRADED HIGH/LOW AS OF 0300 GMT\par  USD/JPY     137.52/54\tab \tab   138.45-137.13\par  USD/DEM     1.7944/46\tab \tab   1.7945-1.7894\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par ---------------------------------------------------------------\par \f28 \par \par \uc2      TOKYO, June 22 (Reuters) - The dollar stayed higher against \par \par \uc2  the yen by midday on Monday after a meeting of Group of Seven \par \par \uc2  (G7) and Asian nations failed to produce a strong accord on \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but its earlier gains were slashed by persistent \par \par \uc2  fears about dollar-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The meeting instead urged \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  to take early action to \par \par \uc2  restore confidence in its banking sector. \par \par \uc2  The dollar closed at 136.65/75 yen and 1.7900/10 marks in New York on Friday. The dollar earlier rose as high as around 138.90 yen in Sydney due to short-covering and speculative purchases. \par \par \uc2  But selling from U.S. operators and options-related sales quickly knocked the dollar down, although the downside was supported by buying interest from importers and investors. \par \par \uc2  A Japanese bank dealer said the dollar could be on an upward bias against the yen amid Japan's poor economic fundamentals and due to uncertainty over how swiftly and clearly it can resolve its banking problems. \par \par \uc2  "I think that the dollar will maintain its upward basis against the yen since it will take time to resolve banking sector problems," said the Japanese bank dealer. \par \par \uc2  A dealer at a U.S. bank said: "The Bank of Japan could step in to sell dollars again if the dollar rises above 140 yen and the Federal Reserve could \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  above 142 yen." \par \par \uc2  Traders said the Japanese government does not want to see the yen falling to 140 yen before the July 12 election, while the United States does not like the yen's quick fall as it could put downward pressure on the Chinese yuan ahead of President Bill Clinton's visit to China on June 25. \par \par \uc2  U.S. Deputy Treasury Secretary Lawrence Summers told a news conference after Saturday's meeting that the joint \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  had given Tokyo a "window of opportunity" to act on its failing economy. \par \par \uc2  Koichi Kato, secretary-general of Japan's ruling Liberal Democratic Party, said on Monday the LDP would come up with details for a so-called bridge bank by July 8. \par \par \uc2  But Kato said the party would like to come up with the details as soon as possible, adding that July 2 - the day the LDP plans to hold its policy-making meeting - may be a "crucial date". \par \par \uc2  Traders were mixed about a near-term direction of the dollar/yen rate. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. bank dealer said if the dollar fell through 137.00 yen, there would be a chance of the dollar's fall to around 135.50 yen. \par \par \uc2  But any sharp fall below 130 yen is unlikely to take place as the United States is not willing to see the yen firm so sharply amid the wobbly U.S. stock market, he said. \par \par \uc2  Vice Finance Minister for International Affairs Eisuke Sakakibara said on Monday that \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets when appropriate. \par \par \uc2  "We will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  when appropriate and we will not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  when it's not appropriate," Sakakibara told reporters as he entered the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Senior Finance Ministry official Haruhiko Kuroda declined comment on Monday on the weakening of the yen since Friday. ((Tokyo Treasury Desk +81-3 3432 1396 tokyo.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010925du6m02cw5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
