\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  View -3: Dlr Seen On Both Sides Of DEM1.8000 \b0\par\par\uc2 487 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 Juni 1998\par 00:31\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  At a press conference following the Tokyo meeting, Summers said questions remain over the issues of transparency in Japan's financial system and how bad assets will be disposed, and market watchers agree that without specifics, the yen will succumb to disillusionment, and the dollar will resume its northward climb. \par \par \uc2  However, analysts focused on Summers' repeated comments that the joint \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  had provided \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  with a "window of opportunity," which combined with the statement welcoming the joint \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  will serve to keep the dollar capped around Y140 next week in the absence of other market-moving news. \par \par \uc2  "I expect that the market will be nervous that the Fed and the BOJ will try to keep that window open as long as is practical," Deutsche Bank's Moloney said. \par \par \uc2  But Rubin doesn't want to face a credibility problem by supporting the yen indefinitely, especially if there are more signs of instability in Japan's financial sector. \par \par \uc2  One such worrying sign is the reports that Long-Term Credit Bank of Japan is in merger talks as it faces an untenable amount of bad loans. LTCB and the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  denied a report Friday that the government might arrange its merger with Nippon Credit Bank Ltd. amid rumors that it was facing serious financial problems. LTCB has repeatedly denied such rumors. \par \par \uc2  Such talk no doubt worries the MOF mandarins, as it provides further impetus to sell the yen. Some believe that just such a sense of crisis is needed to spur Japan in too action, and that by supporting the yen, the U.S. is helping \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  postpone making the difficult decisions necessary. \par \par \uc2  "The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  (by the U.S.) artificially supports the yen and could backfire because it could delay reform," LTCB Warburg's Umetsu said. \par \par \uc2  However, if MOF in the coming days releases a proposal to have banks fully disclose all problem loans, or if it allows a troubled bank to go bust, the markets would react positively as it would be seen as a major step toward streamlining the system. \par \par \uc2  As for the Deutsche mark, the dollar will trade a couple of pfennings or so on either side of DEM1.8000 in the coming week, as market watchers seem to feel that higher interest rates from Germany are still a ways off. \par \par \uc2  Price data coming out of Germany this week "should be fairly tame, indicating that there won't be any rate hikes until the end of the year," Deutsche Bank's Moloney said. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Data on German import prices scheduled to be released Wednesday should\par show a fall of 0.2% for May from the month before, while May producer\par prices should rise 0.2% month-on-month, according to a survey of\par economists by Dow Jones.\par -By John Brinsley; (813) 5255-2929; jbrinsley@ap.org\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (END) Dow Jones Newswires 21-06-98\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 2231GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du6l059wv\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
