\par\par \b \uc2  U.S. Official/Japan -2: Official Traveling With Summers \b0\par\par\uc2 299 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 Juni 1998\par 12:53\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  TOKYO (Dow Jones)--A U.S. government official said Friday that he left meetings with Japanese leaders convinced that "there is a great recognition of the need for action" to clean up Japan's banking problem and stimulate its economy. \par \par \uc2  But the official, who asked not be identified, made clear that the U.S. was still waiting to make sure that Japan followed up its recent pledges of action with concrete policies. \par \par \uc2  "It's actions, not intentions, that are important going forward," the official said. \par \par \uc2  He was traveling to Tokyo with a delegation headed by U.S. Deputy Treasury Secretary Lawrence Summers, who met Friday with Japan's finance minister and \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor, senior executives of the ruling Liberal Democratic Party, and other Japanese officials. \par \par \uc2  The official said Japan had a "window of opportunity" created by recent market developments, an allusion to this week's joint U.S.-\b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the yen. \par \par \uc2  Asked specifically if \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  was now on the right path, the official said: "If I had wanted to use the words `right path,' I'd have worked them into my sentence." \par \par \uc2  He declined to give any specific examples of the kinds of measures that Japan had said it would adopt. \par \par \uc2  Asked about the timing of any imminent Japanese policy announcements, the official said: "The sense of direction that comes out in the period before the election is something that will be watched very closely." Japan will hold elections to its upper house of Parliament on July 12. \par \par \uc2  The official would not address the possibility of possible future \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets, but said: "What is important for \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  over time is fundamentals, and fundamentals depend on policies." \par \par \uc2  (MORE) Dow Jones Newswires 19-06-98 \par \par \uc2  1053GMT \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du6j056rm\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
