\par\par \b \uc2  Taiwan money rates end down on loose funds. \b0\par\par\uc2 410 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 Juni 1998\par 12:34\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TAIPEI, June 19 (Reuters) - Taiwan's money rates ended lower on Friday on the Taiwan dollar's relative stability and loose liquidity in the banking system, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The overnight interbank rate closed at 6.696 percent against Thursday's 6.742 percent finish, with 30-day commercial paper at 6.85 percent against 6.95-7.00. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said U.S.-\b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prop up the yen had helped stabilise the Taiwan dollar, enabling the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to reduce a massive defence of the local unit that had dried up liquidity in the money market. \par \par \uc2  The Taiwan dollar again firmed above T$34 levels in early Friday trade as the closely watched yen stabilised, touching a high of T$33.946. It ended at T$34.073 against Thursday's T$34.101 close. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said because of the yen's stability, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  did not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  heavily in the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has vowed to respect the market's trend and would only \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  on "seasonal and unusual factors." \par \par \uc2  Dealers said due to a relatively loose liquidity as funds flowed back into the banking system, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  decided to advance the due time of a T$10 billion repurchased fund to Friday from July 16. \par \par \uc2  Dealers expected the short-term money rates to fluctuate within the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's target range of 6.75-7.00 percent next week as more funds are scheduled to return to the market. \par \par \uc2  Loosening factors will include the national treasury's transfer of T$35 billion to state banks in salary and retirement payment for military servicemen and veterans on Monday and T$10 billion in interest payments. \par \par \uc2  There will be another T$8 billion in armed forces salary payments on Friday. \par \par \uc2  Tightening factors next week include the maturity of T$33.517 billion in repurchased funds, including T$5.035 billion on Monday, T$6 billion on Tuesday and T$22.482 on Friday. \par \par \uc2  Government bond yields rose as both the stock market and Taiwan dollar market regained confidence. \par \par \uc2  The benchmark seven-year 87/4 bond yield had risen to 6.2075 percent against Thursday's 6.1700 percent, while the 15-year 87/3 bond yield was higher at 6.4025 percent against 6.3775. \par \par \uc2  ((Taipei newsroom, +886 2 2508-0815 fax +886 2 2508-0204, taipei.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010925du6j02o02\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
