\par\par \b \uc2  Japan MOF Tanami: U.S. Shares Same  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  View \b0\par\par\uc2 157 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 Juni 1998\par 10:45\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  TOKYO (Dow Jones)--The top bureaucrat at Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  said Thursday that the coordinated dollar-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the central banks of the U.S. and \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Wednesday sent a strong message to the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. \par \par \uc2  Speaking at a regular press conference, Administrative Vice-Minister Koji Tanami said that Thursday's trading in Tokyo shows that the market has responded positively to Wednesday's action. \par \par \uc2  "The joint \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  shows that \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the U.S. share the same view" regarding the dollar-yen rate, Tanami said. \par \par \uc2  The bureaucrat added that Japan would take additional action in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market if needed. \par \par \uc2  Regarding Friday's scheduled meeting between U.S. Deputy Treasury Secretary Lawrence Summers and Finance Minister Hikaru Matsunaga, Tanami said he expected Japan-U.S. cooperation in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  matters to be reaffirmed. \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 18-06-98 \par \par \uc2  0845GMT \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du6i05c3w\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
