\par\par \b \uc2  Buba/Previous BOJ  \highlight22\uc2 Interventions \highlight\uc2  -2: In Monthly Report \b0\par\par\uc2 232 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 Juni 1998\par 08:34\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  FRANKFURT (Dow Jones)--Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  prior to Wednesday's joint U.S./Japanese efforts to shore up the weak yen were unsuccessful in reversing that trend, the Deutsche Bundesbank said Tuesday in its June monthly report. \par \par \uc2  "The sometimes massive \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  of the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  weren't able to turn around the weakening tendency of the yen," the Bundesbank said, in a report that was written before the coordinated \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the U.S. \par \par \uc2  Wednesday's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  pushed the dollar off its highs against the yen. Around 0630 GMT, the dollar was quoted at Y136.79, up slightly from Y136.64 late Wednesday in New York but down from Y143.23 early Wednesday prior to the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The Bundesbank said the yen's weakening trend due to Japan's recession and conditions in the financial sector had been temporarily stemmed after the announcement of fiscal reforms. \par \par \uc2  Turning to the dollar, the Bundesbank said well-founded, robust U.S. growth, which shows little signs of inflation is the "most important reason for the relatively strong position of the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 " compared with the Deutsche mark. \par \par \uc2  It noted, however, that the "cautious estimates of German economic growth" in the first months of the year are also part of that picture. \pa