\par\par \b \uc2  Asia  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  Roundup: Dlr Dn After  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2 ; Mkt Nervous \b0\par\par\uc2  By John Brinsley \par \uc2 403 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 Juni 1998\par 07:52\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  TOKYO (Dow Jones)--Traders kept nervous watch in Tokyo Thursday, but there was no sign of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  action to prop up the yen after massive joint \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the U.S. and \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  overnight. However, the dollar remained under pressure given its eight-yen plunge the day before, and was slightly lower from its levels late Wednesday in New York. \par \par \uc2  The dollar began Asian trading under siege, but managed to recover on profit-taking by U.S. hedge funds and some buying by Japanese institutional investor. After falling to an early intraday low of Y135.50 around 0002 GMT (8:02 p.m. EDT Wednesday), the dollar came back above Y136, but traders said it could fall further once the London market comes in. \par \par \uc2  But the consensus among traders and analysts was that while the U.S. may have made the surprising decision to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to help the yen and prevent the devaluation of the Chinese yuan (CNY), the dollar remains fundamentally strong against the yen given Tokyo's economic woes. Some expressed surprise that Japan didn't strike while the iron was hot and try to push the dollar down further. \par \par \uc2  "I was surprised that the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  didn't \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the Asian market," said Takashi Nakauchi, \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  manager at Bank of Tokyo-Mitsubishi, who said the overnight \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  had kept him in the office for the past 36 hours. "But it doesn't really matter. This (U.S-\b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  didn't change the trend, it just slowed down the trend of the yen's weakness." \par \par \uc2  But the outlook for the dollar has become more cautious, market watchers agreed. \par \par \uc2  "The message that came out of this is that the U.S. Treasury is prepared to buy, if not Japan, then Asia some time," said Tim Moloney, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Deutsche Bank in Sydney. "It doesn't imply that the U.S.'s strong dollar trend is over." \par \par \uc2  Around 0530 GMT (1:30 a.m. EDT), the dollar is quoted at Y136.19, below Y136.64 late Wednesday in New York and down from Y137.67 late Wednesday in London. The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  also is at DEM1.7835, lower than DEM1.7870 late Wednesday in New York and below DEM1.7860 in London Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) Dow Jones Newswires 18-06-98 \par \par \uc2  0552GMT \par \par \uc2  1034 1863 4162 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du6i05azz\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
