\par\par \b \uc2  Taiwan Ctrl Bk -2: Permanent Solutions Needed For Stable Yen \b0\par\par\uc2 173 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 Juni 1998\par 05:24\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  TAIPEI (Dow Jones)--The joint \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the U.S. and \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  to sell U.S. dollars and boost the yen will "only provide temporary relief for the yen," a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  official said Thursday. \par \par \uc2  In the long term, the yen will stabilize only with "improvements in Japan's economic fundamentals," said Chou A-ting, the director of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  department. \par \par \uc2  The overnight \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  will only temporarily ease the market's expectations that the yen will fall further, while only more permanent solutions to Japan's economic problems are needed to completely stabilize the yen, added Chou. \par \par \uc2  As to the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's own policy, Chou said, in principle, market forces will be allowed to determine the level of the NT dollar. Only when irregular market movements are detected will the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, he added. \par \par \uc2  -By Kirby Chien; 886-2-502-2557; kchien@ap.org \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 18-06-98 \par \par \uc2  0324GMT \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du6i05aj3\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
