\par\par \b \uc2  Early Tokyo: Dlr Rebounds From Lows On US Buys; Mkt Nervous \b0\par\par\uc2 335 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 Juni 1998\par 02:37\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  TOKYO (Dow Jones)--The specter of more \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  kept the dollar under pressure but it had rebounded from early Australasian lows early Thursday in Tokyo as senior Japanese monetary authorities refused to comment on such a possibility. \par \par \uc2  Nevertheless, the dollar is slightly lower than its levels late Wednesday in New York. \par \par \uc2  A day after the U.S. and \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  conducted massive dollar selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the market remained cautious about the possibility of more action by the central banks to support the yen. Early Wednesday in New York trading, the Federal Reserve Bank of New York, acting on behalf of both the Bank of Japan and the U.S. Treasury, sold dollars for yen sending the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to an intraday low of Y136.10. \par \par \uc2  "People are really concerned that the BOJ may step into the market again. That is the real focus of trading (Thursday)," said a Tokyo-based dealer at at European bank. \par \par \uc2  But short-covering buying by U.S. funds brought the dollar back up after it hit an early low of Y135.50 at 0002 GMT (8:02 p.m. EDT Wednesday). \par \par \uc2  The market may also have been temporarily calmed by the refusal to comment on the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by Eisuke Sakakibara, vice minister for international affairs at \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2 . However, the head of MOF's international finance bureau, Haruhiko Kuroda, said he hoped that the market would appreciate the message of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Around 0030 GMT, the dollar is trading at Y136.40, up from Y135.82 around 0001 GMT but below Y136.64 in New York late Wednesday. It was at Y143.23 late in Tokyo Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is also trading at DEM1.7860, higher than DEM1.7822 earlier but below DEM1.7870 late Wednesday in New York. The dollar was at DEM1.7955 in Tokyo late Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) Dow Jones Newswires 18-06-98 \par \par \uc2  0037GMT \par \par \uc2  1074 1863 4162 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du6i059ob\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
