\par\par \b \uc2  Asian Crisis At A Glance:Dlr Rises Slightly;No  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 473 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 Juni 1998\par 13:14\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  -- Traders watched nervously in Tokyo, but there was no sign of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  action Thursday to prop up the yen after massive joint \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  Wednesday by the U.S. and \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 . At 1100 GMT, the U.S. dollar was at Y136.74, up from Y136.64 late Wednesday in New York. [*R/JA] \par \par \uc2  -- Southeast Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  rose sharply in line with the yen's rally, but stabilized as dollar-buying interest emerged at new levels. The Indonesian rupiah remained very weak with poor sentiment, trading at IDR15,700 at 0745 GMT. \par \par \uc2  -- Tokyo stocks rallied on the yen's surge; the Nikkei rose more than 600 points to end 4.4% higher. [*R/JA] \par \par \uc2  Other Asian stock indexes soared on news of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The South Korean exchange led the recovery with a 7.1% rise; Malaysia's rose 6.8%; the Philippines' rose 6.5%, Hong Kong's rose 6.4% and Thailand's was up 6.9%. \par \par \uc2  -- Japan posted a merchandise trade surplus of Y1.219 trillion in May, up 67% from May 1997 and the 14th straight month the trade surplus has risen on year. [*R/JA] \par \par \uc2  -- South Korea's Financial Supervisory Commission unveiled 55 companies on the "black list" of companies deemed nonviable, including 20 belonging to Korea's five largest conglomerates - Hyundai, Samsung, Daewoo, LG and SK. [*R/SK] \par \par \uc2  -- China Vice Minister of Foreign Trade Sun refuted a report that China would consider devaluing the yuan if the weakening yen caused its exports to plunge, official media said. Foreign Ministry spokesman Zhu said he welcomed the stronger yen and reaffirmed China's commitment not to devalue the yuan, calling that stance China's contribution to financial stability in Asia. \par \par \uc2  Adding value to exports and restructuring businesses are the solution to a strong yuan, not devaluation, Chinese trading company executives said. [*R/CH] \par \par \uc2  -- The Indonesian government and Japan's Export-Import Bank signed a $1 billion loan to boost Indonesia's exports, part of Japan's emergency economic package to stabilize Southeast Asian economies. [*R/IO] [*R/JA] \par \par \uc2  -- The Philippines may be the only Southeast Asian country to post GDP growth in 1998, the U.S.-based Institute of International Finance said. [*R/RP] \par \par \uc2  -- Japan's government and Liberal Democratic Party may announce permanent income tax cuts prior to the upper house elections July 12, the Nihon Keizai Shimbun reported. [*R/JA] \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par               Stock Index                       \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par                          Change      Level     Thursday Friday\par Hong Kong  Hang Seng     Up 511.62  8,515.97  HK$7.7430 HK$7.7443\par Indonesisa Jakarta Comp  Up 20.651  440.093   IDR14,650 IDR16,550\par Japan      Nikkei        Up 646.16 15,361.54  Y136.64  Y136.74\par S. Korea   Kospi         Up  21.68  325.49   KRW1,392 KRW1,420\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (END) Dow Jones Newswires 18-06-98\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 1114GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1042 4190 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du6i056po\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
