\par\par \b \uc2  Dollar moves narrowly after paring earlier losses. \b0\par\par\uc2 378 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 Juni 1998\par 07:28\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      TOKYO, June 18 (Reuters) - ASIAN \b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2  ACTIVITY: \par \par \uc2      0525 GMT -- \par \par \uc2      *Dollar moved narrowly above 136 yen in mid-afternoon \par \par \uc2  Tokyo, sandwiched by solid bids and offers from Japanese \par \par \uc2  investors. \par \par \uc2      *But greenback's upside seen heavy due to concerns over \par \par \uc2  more dollar-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by central banks. \par \par \uc2      *Dollar/yen at 136.15/20, down slightly from midday's \par \par \uc2  136.30/35. \par \par \uc2      *"Activity is a lot brisker than the impression you might \par \par \uc2  get from watching price moves," said a dealer at a trust bank. \par \par \uc2  *Dealers said dollar/yen's outlook remained mixed after sharp overnight fall. \par \par \uc2  *"Those who believe the yen's weak trend is unchanged are willing to bargain-hunt the dollar. But those who fear a further dollar drop are looking to sell for hedging purposes," the trust bank dealer said. \par \par \uc2  *Market cautious ahead of planned news conference by Prime Minister Ryutaro Hashimoto at 0730 GMT, and talks between U.S. Deputy Treasury Secretary Lawrence Summers and Vice Finance Minister for International Affairs Eisuke Sakakibara later on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  0318 GMT - *Dollar was off its low against the yen by Tokyo midday on Thursday on substantial bargain-hunting demand, but it stayed under downward pressure due to lingering concern over \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers said. \par \par \uc2  *Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  action had not been detected so far on Thursday, but concern over \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was growing should dollar/yen rally gain speed, they said. \par \par \uc2  *The market was also turning cautious about building fresh postions ahead of U.S. Deputy Treasury Secretary Lawrence Summers arrival in Japan later on Thursday and the Group of Seven (G7) deputies meeting scheduled on Saturday. \par \par \uc2  *"Many operators are expecting the BOJ to step in if the dollar rises rapidly. In this mood, bidders were very careful and speculators were quickly taking profits even at minor rallies," a foreign bank dealer said. \par \par \uc2  *The U.S. Federal Reserve of New York and the BOJ jointly \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  overnight and were estimated to have spent as much as $6 billion selling dollars for yen in New York overnight. \par \par \uc2  *The surprising joint effort by the U.S. and Japan hammered down the dollar by more than six yen overnight. ((Tokyo Treasury Desk +81-3 3432-9780 tokyo.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010925du6i02rms\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
