\par\par \b \uc2  Taiwan dollar ends sharply higher on yen rebound. \b0\par\par\uc2 267 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 Juni 1998\par 10:20\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TAIPEI, June 18 (Reuters) - The Taiwan dollar closed sharply higher on Thursday, responding to a firming Japanese yen after the United States and \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  launched joint \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prop up the troubled yen, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The Taiwan dollar, which rose as high as T$33.951 in early trade, ended at T$34.101 against its Wednesday T$34.681 finish. \par \par \uc2  Turnover through dealers was heavy at US$518.5 million. \par \par \uc2  Taiwan's second \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market Cosmos \b \highlight22\uc2 Foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  also closed higher at T$34.100 against Wednesday's T$34.775 finish. On the Cosmos market, the dollar saw a high of T$33.800 and a low of T$34.220. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the U.S. dollar's weakness triggered some demand. "There were a lot of buyers in the market today because the price was so good," one dealer said. \par \par \uc2  Dealers noted the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's presence on Thursday, but this time on both sides of the trading table. \par \par \uc2  "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was out there today to make up for all the U.S. dollars it had sold. It took some profits too," the dealer said. \par \par \uc2  Dealers saw a stable range of T$34.1-T$34.4 for Friday. \par \par \uc2  Some dealers said they did not expect the yen's rebound would last without further \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "\b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's economic fundamentals are still very poor," another dealer said. ((Taipei newsroom, +886 2 2508-0815 fax +886 2 2508-0204, taipei.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     **..all news on Taiwan\tab    China\tab    Hong Kong\tab .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (C) Reuters Limited 1998.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010925du6i02rhm\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
