\par\par \b \uc2  Dlr/yen calm in Europe,  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  nerves linger. \b0\par\par\uc2 534 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 Juni 1998\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, June 18 (Reuters) - The dollar was steady against the yen in morning Europe, up from overnight lows but still nursing its wounds from Wednesday's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  action to support the Japanese unit. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said activity was relatively calm in early trade amid lingering jitters over further \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The outcome of U.S. Deputy Treasury Secretary Lawrence Summers' visit to Japan as well as a weekend meeting of G7 deputies was also keeping yen bears on the defensive. \par \par \uc2  "The market is in wait-and-see mode at the moment," said James McKay, economist at Commonwealth Bank of Australia. \par \par \uc2  "The market will be reluctant about taking the dollar higher and testing \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  resolve and it wants to see what will come out of the Japan meetings." \par \par \uc2  The Federal Reserve and the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  jointly \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to sell dollars for yen on Wednesday and were estimated to have spent as much as $6 billion to turn the yen around. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  impact saw the dollar pushed down to 135.50 yen overnight, its lowest point in more than three weeks, and more than 10 yen below Tuesday's near eight-year high of 146.75. \par \par \uc2  It managed to recover some ground into morning Europe, steadying at 136.80/90 yen by 0755 GMT. \par \par \uc2  Summers will be meeting senior Japanese officials on his Tokyo visit, including Finance Minister Hikaru Matsunaga on Friday, before attending a G7 deputy finance ministers meeting Saturday which is also in Tokyo. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said these meetings will try to maintain the momentum of yen support and may even yield further steps by Japan to stimulate its economy. Without such steps and when the threat of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  recedes, the yen could head lower again. \par \par \uc2  "Fundamentals still don't support the yen and the U.S. still doesn't have an interest to weaken the dollar," said Steve Barrow, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Bear Stearns in London. \par \par \uc2  "The reason for U.S. cooperation to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  was to stop Asia from sliding into the abyss, but as the threat of Fed action fades, dollar/yen will start creeping higher." \par \par \uc2  Dollar/mark was also steady, ticking above its early lows. The West German IFO business climate index for May came out at 98.7m unchanged from the April level and in line with analysts' expectations. \par \par \uc2  The Bundesbank's monthly report, meantime, gave an upbeat assessment of the German economy, highlighting broad-based growth. Dealers said this rekindled speculation of higher German interest rates. \par \par \uc2  Dollar/mark stood at 1.7835/40 in morning trade, down from an earlier top of 1.7878 marks. It stood at 1.7887/92 late Wednesday in Europe. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the market was now eyeing U.S. trade data for April due at 1230 GMT. An average of analysts' forecasts point to a $13.4 billion deficit from a $13.0 bln shortfall in March. \par \par \uc2  "The market has been watching the trade data more closely recently but today's numbers will be overshadowed by the preoccupation with \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said a U.S. bank dealer. \par \par \uc2  ((Andrew Reierson, London newsroom +44 171 542 6745, uk.\b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2 .news@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par 