\par\par \b \uc2  Japan trade surplus surges as weak demand hits imports. \b0\par\par\uc2 408 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 Juni 1998\par 03:35\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, June 18 (Reuters) - Japan's customs-cleared trade surplus surged in May as imports declined due to weak domestic demand and higher exports to Europe failed to offset the large decline from ailing Asia, economists said Thursday. \par \par \uc2  The surplus climbed 66.6 percent in May from a year ago to 1.22 trillion yen ($8.9 billion), the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  said. \par \par \uc2  Japan's politically sensitive trade surplus with the United States rose to 455.43 billion yen ($3.3 billion) in May, up 41.0 percent from a year earlier, it said. The figures were not adjusted for seasonal factors. \par \par \uc2  The May trade surplus - the 14th consecutive month of year-on-year rises - was slightly higher than the predictions of economists, who expected a 57 percent rise to 1.15 trillion yen ($8.4 billion). \par \par \uc2  "The data is a clear reflection of the impact from the economic downturn in other Asian countries. The rise in exports to the United States and Europe was not sufficient to offset the drop in exports to Asia. The main reason behind the rise in the surplus is the poor domestic economy," said Hisashi Yamada, an economist at the Japan Research Institute Ltd. \par \par \uc2  Japan's trade with Asia fell 28.3 percent to 406.56 billion yen ($2.9 billion), but its trade with the European Union rose 94.2 percent to 394.03 billion yen ($2.9 billion), the data showed. \par \par \uc2  A ministry official told reporters the ministry expects the pace of the rise in the surplus to slow gradually as the economy recovers on the government's economic stimulus package, whose impact is expected to appear around the autumn. \par \par \uc2  Jason James, head of research at HSBC Securities Japan Ltd, told Reuters Television that the rise in the overall surplus should help aid the yen's recovery in the short term. The yen rose sharply after joint \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the United States and \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Wednesday. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  traders virtually ignored the data, but the dollar fell below 136 yen in early Tokyo trade on stop-loss dollar sales and strong fears that Bank of Japan could continue to sell dollars for yen. \par \par \uc2  U.S. Deputy Treasury Secretary Lawrence Summers was due to arrive in Tokyo to discuss Japan's economic problems with his Japanese counterpart, Eisuke Sakakibara, before an expected meeting of Group of Seven financial deputies. \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010925du6i02r50\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
