\par\par \b \uc2  Early Taiwan dlr rises above T$34 on yen rebound. \b0\par\par\uc2 293 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 Juni 1998\par 03:26\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TAIPEI, June 18 (Reuters) - The Taiwan dollar was sharply higher, rising above T$34 in early Thursday trade following a joint U.S./\b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  which propped the yen up to 136.75 in overnight trade, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  At 0115 GMT the Taiwan dollar was quoted at T$33.990 against its Thursday T$34.681 finish. In the first fifteen minutes of trade the Taiwan dollar had touched T$34.951 at its highest point. \par \par \uc2  Turnover through dealers was heavy at US$74 million. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the joint \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by U.S. and \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  in overnight trade had helped pull the Taiwan dollar up, but at the same time they did not expect the local unit to move above T$33.5 to the U.S. dollar. \par \par \uc2  "I don't see it going any higher than T$33.5, unless the yen rises higher," one dealer said. \par \par \uc2  "When the yen was around 136 before, the Taiwan dollar was roughly at T$33.8," another dealer said. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said that demand was still strong for the greenback from ordinary \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  players, and they expected the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to be in the market buying back U.S. dollars as well. \par \par \uc2  "Although the yen has rebounded, there is nothing about Japan's economy that says the yen will continue to rise," the dealer said. \par \par \uc2  Taiwan's second \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market Cosmos \b \highlight22\uc2 Foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  was also trading higher in early morning trade. The second market opened at T$34.000 and was trading between T$33.960-990, against Wednesday's T$34.775 finish. ((Taipei newsroom, +886 2 2508-0815 fax +886 2 2508-0204, taipei.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010925du6i02r4q\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
