\par\par \b \uc2  Dollar capped vs yen in Tokyo on caution over BOJ. \b0\par\par\uc2 475 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 Juni 1998\par 03:48\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      TOKYO, June 18 (Reuters) - ASIAN \b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2  ACTIVITY: \par \par \uc2      0140 GMT --*Dollar stayed under downward pressure against \par \par \uc2  yen in mid-morning Tokyo on Thursday as concern over \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  limited active buying. \par \par \uc2      *BOJ action not detected so far this morning, but concerns \par \par \uc2  over \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  growing should dollar/yen's \par \par \uc2  rally gain speed, dealers said. \par \par \uc2      *U.S. Federal Reserve and Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  (BOJ) jointly \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  overnight and estimated to have spent as much as $6 \par \par \uc2  billion selling dollars for yen in New York. \par \par \uc2  *Dollar well-supported on bids from Japanese importers and exporters. A major U.S. hedge fund also rumoured to have bought dollars below 136 yen. \par \par \uc2  *A senior Japanese Finance Ministry official said cooperation with United States on \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  continuing. \par \par \uc2  *The official also said G7 deputies and Manila Framework countries to hold meeting in Tokyo on Saturday and topic will be on Manila Framework meeting policy challenges in Asia. \par \par \uc2  *Japanese Vice Finance Minister for International Affairs Eisuke Sakakibara and U.S. Deputy Treasury Secretary Lawrence Summers likely to have talks in Tokyo later on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  *Dollar at 136.10/20 yen against 136.90/00 in late New York on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  2354 GMT \par \par \uc2  *Dollar fell below 136 yen in early Tokyo trade on stop-loss dollar sales and strong fears that Bank of Japan (BOJ) could continue to sell dollars for yen after United States and \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  jointly \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prop up yen overnight. \par \par \uc2  *Stop-loss dollar sales were triggered at 136.00 yen and sent dollar down, with further stop-loss sales and options-related sales expected, said a trust bank dealer. \par \par \uc2  *"While short-term operators are willing to sell dollars, long-term investors are likely to take a wait-and-see stance during morning trade," said a trust bank dealer. \par \par \uc2  *There was talk of commercial dollar buying expected at 0100 GMT, which could support the dollar. \par \par \uc2  *A dealer at a European bank said stop-loss dollar sales seen at 135.50 yen and there was a perception that the BOJ may be willing to push dollar down below 135 yen. \par \par \uc2  *Traders said BOJ \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  not detected so far, but trading was nervous amid fear of BOJ action. \par \par \uc2  *A senior \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealer at Japanese bank said Japanese investor dollar buying interest remained solid and weak yen trend had not altered. Investors expected to step in to buy dollars once downward moves show signs of coming to halt. \par \par \uc2  *"Japan's policy will come into a spotlight again after the concerted \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said the dealer. \par \par \uc2  *Traders said \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  would be forced to speed up cleaning up its banking system and the stimulation of its economy in return for U.S. help to support the sagging yen. ((Tokyo Treasury Desk +81-3 3432 8785 tokyo.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010925du6i02r19\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\