\par\par \b \uc2  Tokyo stocks soar, dollar cautious on BOJ. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Hiroko Nakata \par \uc2 622 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 Juni 1998\par 02:25\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, June 18 (Reuters) - Tokyo share prices jumped over four percent on Thursday on the back of a sharply higher yen that found new strength from a surprise wave of overnight \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The stock market's main barometer, the 225-share Nikkei average, jumped 4.39 percent, or 646.16 points, to 15,361.54, cheered by the yen's rise. It was above the 15,000 level for the first time since last Friday. \par \par \uc2  Share prices have been battered by concern about \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's economy and the health of its financial institutions. \par \par \uc2  "\b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  will only have a temporary effect on the market (if it is not backed up by sound policy steps)," said Hiroshi Arano, a general manager of Dai-Ichi Kangyo Asahi Asset Management Co. "But it virtually means that Japanese policies will be monitored by G7 (Group of Seven) countries," he said. \par \par \uc2  A consensus in the market is that Japan promised steps to cheer up the economy and its troubled banking sector in return for U.S. support for the ailing yen. \par \par \uc2  On Wednesday, the United States and Japan moved to halt a nosedive in the battered Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  which had threatened to push Asia into a fresh round of crisis. \par \par \uc2  Joining forces with Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the Treasury Department instructed the New York Federal Reserve on Wednesday to spend an estimated $2 billion to buy the yen, the first such U.S. action on behalf of the yen in more than six years. \par \par \uc2  The dollar, which rose to an eight-year high of above 146 yen earlier in the week, plunged to 136 yen in New York on the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and was trading at about 136.90 yen in late-afternoon Tokyo trading. \par \par \uc2  "Many operators are expecting the BOJ to step in if the dollar rises rapidly. In this mood, bidders were very careful and speculators were quickly taking profits even at minor rallies," a foreign bank \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealer said. \par \par \uc2  Finance Minister Hikaru Matsunaga said on Thursday that the joint \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was a "decisive" step. No follow-up \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  action was detected in the market so far on Thursday in Tokyo, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Japanese government bond prices and futures prices meanwhile fell after the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  joint \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  fueled expectations that \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  may consider drastic income tax cuts. \par \par \uc2  U.S. President Bill Clinton and Prime Minister Ryutaro Hashimoto talked about \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's economy by telephone just hours before the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  began. \par \par \uc2  Traders said that no sharp dollar rise was likely ahead of visit by U.S. Deputy Treasury Secretary Lawrence Summers to Japan later on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Summers is likely to hold talks with Vice Finance Minister for International Affairs Eisuke Sakakibara later on Thursday and also meet Matsunaga from 11.50 a.m. (0250 GMT) on Friday, ministry officials said. \par \par \uc2  News of the joint \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  hit nervous \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets only hours before Summers was due to leave for Tokyo for hastily convened crisis talks with Japanese counterparts on the economic situation in Japan and elsewhere in troubled Asia. \par \par \uc2  He will also attend a meeting of deputy finance ministers from the Group of Seven industrial nations and from nations that take part in the Manila framework on Saturday. \par \par \uc2  The sagging yen and the decline of Japan's economy, which has entered a recession, put additional economic pressure on already struggling nations across the Asian continent. \par \par \uc2  Fears had grown that weak yen would set off a new round of devaluations across Asia, particularly in China, whose ability to stand firm is seen as key to containing Asia's crisis. ((Tokyo Newsroom +81-3 3432 8018 tokyo.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010925du6i02r0j\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
