\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  IN EUROPE-Yen kept afloat by  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  fear. \b0\par\par\uc2 702 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 Juni 1998\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, June 18 (Reuters) - The yen pared gains against other major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Thursday, but its slippage from post-\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  peaks is unlikely to extend much further before officials from the Group of Seven nations meet, analysts said. \par \par \uc2  Tuesday's joint purchases of yen by the U.S. and Japanese authorities drove the yen to four-week highs against the dollar and a one-month high against the mark overnight. \par \par \uc2  While the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  steadied below these peaks in Europe, shell-shocked traders were reluctant to bet against it, particularly before a meeting of G7 finance officials in Tokyo this weekend. \par \par \uc2  "People are dazed and given that some traders are still long of dollars, any rally (in dollar/yen) will be sold into," said Paul Coughlin, chief trader at American Express Bank in London. \par \par \uc2  "The mentality may be that central banks can't buck the trend but it depends on how deep their pockets are. People are afraid that if they try and take them on they will just get slapped down again." \par \par \uc2  The dollar was at 136.78/88 yen at 1410 GMT from the overnight low of 135.50, which was 7.7 percent below the near-eight-year highs set only three days ago. That compares with 137.87/97 late in Europe on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  Mark/yen was at 76.60/63 from 77.08/11 late in Europe on Wednesday and about five percent below Monday's 5-3/4-year peak. \par \par \uc2  Comments by European central bankers on Thursday helped to dull some of the impact of Wednesday's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Bundesbank council members Reimut Jochimsen and Franz-Christoph Zeitler said \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was no substitute for reform in \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Jochimsen also said Japan had to implement reforms to avoid \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  devaluations in China and Hong Kong. \par \par \uc2  Meantime, Swiss National Bank board member Bruno Gehrig said it would be naive to think that \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  alone would not solve \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's problems. \par \par \uc2  Although \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  fears continue to persist, such views will carry more weight if Japan officials do not come up with new measures to stimulate growth after they meet U.S. Deputy Treasury Secretary Lawrence Summers and after the G7 meeting. \par \par \uc2  "We still need to see more tax cuts and economic reforms implemented in Japan before the weak yen trend will change," said James McKay, economist at Commonwealth Bank of Australia. \par \par \uc2  Meantime, the dollar was hobbled against the mark as an upbeat assessment of German growth by the Bundesbank triggered talk of higher German interest rates. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said the economic upturn had gathered pace and become more broad-based. \par \par \uc2  The dollar was at 1.7894/00 marks at 1424 GMT from 1.7887/92 late yesterday. \par \par \uc2  Despite this pick up in German growth, a report on Thursday showed that the U.S. trade deficit with Western Europe widened in April. While the bilateral deficit with Japan shrank, the overall shortfall rising to a larger-than-expected $14.46 billion, the largest on record. \par \par \uc2  This was expected to weigh on the dollar in the longer term. \par \par \uc2  "The U.S. trade deficit is a big negative for the dollar," Gerard Lyons, economist at DKB International, told Reuters Television. \par \par \uc2  The only support dollar/mark received on Thursday came from gains sterling racked up against the German \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The pound raced to one-and-a-half-month highs against the mark and rose against the dollar as expectations of higher UK interest rates were fanned by a report showing British retail sales leaped by 1.7 percent in May, more than double expectations. \par \par \uc2  "The danger is that (sterling/mark) will test back through 3.0, and if it gets through there, move back up to 3.02 or even 3.05," said Neil Parker, treasury economist at Royal Bank of Scotland. "But this will be a short-term move and should be unsustainable." \par \par \uc2  Sterling was at 2.9971/78 marks at 1437 GMT from 2.9725/35 late in Europe on Wednesday. It was at $1.6743/48 from $1.6611/21 late yesterday. ((Swaha Pattanaik, London newsroom, +44 171 542 6284, uk.\b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2 .news@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010925du6i02nxr\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
