\par\par \b \uc2  Screen-based  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  increased impact-dealers. \b0\par\par\uc2 555 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 Juni 1998\par 16:06\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, June 18 (Reuters) - The U.S. Federal Reserve and Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  probably sped up the impact of their \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Wednesday by placing dollar/yen sales orders on the EBS screen-based dealing system, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The two central banks stepped in to buy the ailing yen on Wednesday. Their \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the ensuing market stampede out of dollar/yen pushed the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  down by more than six percent by Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Traders in New York and London said the Federal Reserve's dollar sales, which started as the North American session was just beginning, came through both the traditional method of interbank brokers and through the EBS Partnership's Electronic Broking System. \par \par \uc2  "If they (the central banks) wanted anonymity, EBS would be the worse thing to use because there's no confidentiality at all," said one dealer at a U.S. bank. \par \par \uc2  "But for their purposes at the moment, EBS is probably a good tool for them to use...because they need to be seen to be \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2 ." \par \par \uc2  In screen-based \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealing - a transaction network based on electronic systems which has been in use for more than five years - any party in a transaction can be identified through a dealing code. \par \par \uc2  While the traders are unaware of their counterparty until after the transaction, they will know once the deal has gone through. \par \par \uc2  Some traders say this could be a more certain way to let the market know that a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  because there is no attempt at anonymity. \par \par \uc2  "The word spreads as fast as it ever did through the brokers," said one broker in London. But he added: "A disadvantage of EBS is you may hit some banks you did not want to hit at that time." \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  through electronic broking can also be more cost-efficient for the central banks because they can signal their intention to defend a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  with fewer deals, and hence at less cost, than through broker-based \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Some, meanwhile, said the Federal Reserve may have used different methods for the yen buying done on its own account and the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on behalf of the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "There seems to be some understanding in the market that the orders that the Fed put through EBS were those on behalf of the BOJ, and that the orders placed by phone were the ones on its own account," said one trader at a Japanese bank in London. \par \par \uc2  Both the U.S. Treasury Department and Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  confirmed on Wednesday that the concerted \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  had taken place, and some dealers placed the volume of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar/yen selling at $6 billion. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  drove dollar/yen down from Wednesday's session high of 144.09 yen to the day's trough at 136.00, and the slide extended into Thursday. \par \par \uc2  At 1215 GMT the dollar was quoted at 136.67/77 yen, up from a 3-1/2-week low of 135.50 yen reached in the overnight Asian session. The low meant dollar/yen had dropped by 7.7 percent from the near-eight-year high of 146.75 it reached on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  ((Chizu Nomiyama, London newsroom, +44 171-542-6721, uk.\b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2 .news@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010925du6i02lqr\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
