\par\par \b \uc2  Taiwan stocks end up 4 pct on yen, global rallies. \b0\par\par\uc2 492 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 Juni 1998\par 06:22\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      TAIPEI, June 18 (Reuters) - Taiwan share prices rallied to \par \par \uc2  close 4.04 percent higher on Thursday as the market joined Wall \par \par \uc2  Street and other Asian markets to cheer U.S./\b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  joint \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's troubled yen, brokers said. \par \par \uc2      * Close: up 301.93 points/4.04 percent at 7,768.31 \par \par \uc2      * Turnover: active at T$149.12 bln vs T$129.13 bln \par \par \uc2      * The U.S./\b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  joint \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prop up the yen \par \par \uc2  brought relief to the markets in the United States, Europe, and \par \par \uc2  across the region, spurring across-the-board buying. \par \par \uc2      * Trend-setting electronics and plastics led the rally, with \par \par \uc2  many shares surging by the daily seven percent limit. \par \par \uc2      The benchmark stock index jumped 2.57 percent at the open \par \par \uc2  and kept on rising to hit an intra-day high of 7,771.76 points \par \par \uc2  -- a 4.09 percent rise, reflecting growing optimisim, brokers \par \par \uc2  said. \par \par \uc2      The index slid a bit to finish with a 4.04 percent rise, \par \par \uc2  marking the fourth consecutive day of gains. \par \par \uc2      The index had risen 651.2 points, or 9.15 percent, so far \par \par \uc2  this week. \par \par \uc2      "This is another roller-coaster ride. The good news is this \par \par \uc2  time we are going up," Nomura Securities' analyst Chris Hsieh \par \par \uc2  said. \par \par \uc2      Trend-setting electronics shares surged 5.94 percent, \par \par \uc2  followed by plastics, which rose 5.4 percent. \par \par \uc2      Many technology shares were limit up after active trade, \par \par \uc2  thanks to renewed confidence. Microchip maker United \par \par \uc2  Microelectronics  rose T$2.9 to T$44.5, while rival \par \par \uc2  Taiwan Semicondocutor  - a leading blue chip and \par \par \uc2  watched market barometer - advanced T$5 to T$79.5. \par \par \uc2  "Because the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was unexpected, its impact is \par \par \uc2  huge," Allen Huang, vice president of National Securities. "The \par \par \uc2  unexpected move removes most of the uncertainty in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2  market." \par \par \uc2      Taiwan officials hailed the coordinated \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \par \par \uc2  United States and \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2      Taiwan \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  chief Chou Ah-ting \par \par \uc2  said the yen's rise helped eliminate what he called anticipatory \par \par \uc2  sentiment in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. Finance Minister Paul Chiu \par \par \uc2  said the move would help Taiwan economy and markets. \par \par \uc2  The Taiwan dollar reacted favourably to the yen's strength, \par \par \uc2  rising strongly to T$34.085 at 0400 GMT against Wednesday's \par \par \uc2  T$34.681 close. \par \par \uc2      But some brokers said they still had some doubt whether the \par \par \uc2  yen's rally would last. \par \par \uc2      "There is no question that the United States and Japan are \par \par \uc2  determined to stop the yen's fall at the moment. But as long as \par \par \uc2  Japan's economy remains weak, the yen is still under pressure," \par \par \uc2  Nomura's Hsieh said. \par \par \uc2  "We cannot be too optimistic," he said. \par \par \uc2  Brokers also said profit-taking pressure is likely to \par \par \uc2  emerge after four days of rises. \par \par \uc2  For Friday, a range of 7,700-7,900 was seen. \par \par \uc2  ((Taipei newsroom, +886 2 2508-0815 fax +886 2 2508-0204, \par \par \uc2  taipei.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010925du6i02k1e\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
