\par\par \b \uc2  U.S. Dlr Sales A Modest Confidence Vote In Japan Reforms \b0\par\par\uc2  By William Murray \par \uc2 391 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 Juni 1998\par 23:32\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  WASHINGTON (Dow Jones)--The Clinton administration's first dollars sales are a modest vote of confidence in Japanese Prime Minister Ryutaro Hashimoto's pledge to reform his nation's troubled economy, officials say. \par \par \uc2  But there are still signs of uncertainty in Washington about reform implementation, including Treasury Secretary Robert Rubin's continued refrain that action on structural banking reforms by Japan will be critical for the long-run health of the yen. \par \par \uc2  The dispatching of Deputy Treasury Secretary Lawrence Summers to Tokyo with New York Federal Reserve President William McDonough for a series of meetings with top finance and \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  officials in Japan, along with certain political leaders, is also aimed partly at driving home the reform implementation message. \par \par \uc2  And Federal Reserve Chairman Alan Greenspan is also expected to visit Tokyo after parliamentary elections on July 12 to compare notes with authorities on reforms, and potentially to urge more rapid implementation, if necessary. \par \par \uc2  Though pre-election uncertainties are bound to persist about Japan's policy commitments, indications among officials in Washington are that the U.S. still backed joint \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  with \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  to show markets that there are signs of commitment in Tokyo and policy inertia may be abating. \par \par \uc2  President Clinton, who spoke with Hashimoto for about 30 minutes overnight and prior to the joint \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , told reporters Wednesday that his level of confidence in the reform process has been raised. \par \par \uc2  "I was very encouraged by the prime minister's statement that he intends to pursue aggressive reform of their banking institutions, and intends to do the things that were necessary to get that economy going again," Clinton said. "And therefore, I thought it was important that we support them." \par \par \uc2  Treasury Secretary Rubin and top aides also had a series of high-level contacts over recent days, in which Japanese officials offered broader details about reform plans, and built confidence within the Treasury to enable Rubin to sign off on \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  What is also clear from the first \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the U.S. against its own \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  since 1992 is that the Clinton administration is concerned about a buildup of potentially unbridled financial market strains in Asia, including the potential for runaway \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  troubles. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) Dow Jones Newswires 17-06-98 \par \par \uc2  2132GMT \par \par \uc2  4234 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du6h05955\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
